Apply link-time HLSL-to-Vulkan layout options, and report options a link cannot apply.

IComponentType::linkWithOptions accepts any CompilerOptionName and loads the entries into the
linked component type's option set. TargetProgram (source/slang/slang-target-program.cpp) merges
that set over the target's into m_optionSet, but TargetProgram::getHLSLToVulkanLayoutOptions
returned the target request's HLSLToVulkanLayoutOptions, built from the session's and the target's
option sets only. Every option those layout options carry is therefore ignored at link time:
VulkanUseEntryPointName, which works on the session or the target, still names the SPIR-V entry
point "main" when given to linkWithOptions. Capability and Profile are fixed on the target request
when the session creates it, and code generation reads the target's capabilities, so given at link
time they change nothing either (spirv_1_6 still emits SPIR-V 1.5). Nothing is reported for any of
them.

This builds the program's own HLSLToVulkanLayoutOptions from its merged option set when the program
carries options of its own, and warns E00136 link-time-option-has-no-effect, when code is generated, for a program that
carries Capability or Profile from linkWithOptions. A program without options of its own uses the target request's
layout options as before. A regression test is added as
tools/slang-unit-test/unit-test-link-time-options.cpp.

Measured on v2026.14.1 by diffing the emitted SPIR-V: Optimization and FloatingPointMode take effect
at link time; VulkanUseEntryPointName and Capability change nothing and report nothing.
